      "side": 1,
      "message": "My case that reproduced the TIMED_OUT(-110) error was the call from system_server to audioserver after Car Service has crashed while radio playback ongoing (HwAudioSource.start()):\n\n(system_server binder) AudioSystem::registerPolicyMixes() -\u003e \n    (audioserver binder - \"the caller\") AudioPolicyManager::unregisterPolicyMixes() -\u003e\n        (audioserver audiopolicy command thread) AudioFlinger::createAudioPatch()\n\nBut it can be also simply the case while starting audio source where binder call to AudioPolicyManager::startAudioSource() -\u003e connectAudioSource() involves audio patches creation.\nSo I will put this as example in this commit msg.\n\nBTW, I have put detailed analysis of my case into: https://partnerissuetracker.corp.google.com/issues/356095582\n* currently the description might be hardly readable, have to format it (but not able to edit it right now)",
      "parentUuid": "55291974_09da48dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 45,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "cb537560f7e42ca127d7b7507b68151e6636f73c",
