      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-20T00:09:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The risk here is that if the original call comes via Binder, there is a 5 s timeout enforced by TimeCheck to complete the operation. Since we have already waited for 3 s (from my understanding), if the release takes unexpectedly long time, the audio server process will crash due to TimeCheck. We should better make the patch release asynchronously.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2164,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2164,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "cb537560f7e42ca127d7b7507b68151e6636f73c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "552df4db_5c0f3559",
        "filename": "services/audiopolicy/service/AudioPolicyService.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 2164,
      "author": {
        "id": 3225096
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-29T17:24:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After 3s timeout in AudioCommandThread process, the binder process (whose transaction is being monitored by mentioned 5s TimeCheck) gets unblocked (so far binder was awaiting 3s in AudioPolicyService::AudioCommandThread::sendCommand() for CREATE_AUDIO_PATCH cmd result) and executes further asynchronously (has 5-3\u003d2s remaining to finalize the transaction). Since this (emergency/fallback) call to af-\u003ereleaseAudioPatch() is done from AudioCommandThread process, it does not affect binder process.",
      "parentUuid": "37ccb8fb_e6b12061",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2164,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2164,
        "endChar": 65
      },
