      "writtenOn": "2024-08-15T22:42:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, I see, indeed here \u0027sendCommand\u0027 times out after 3s and returns the control back to the Binder thread handling the transaction: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/av/services/audiopolicy/service/AudioPolicyService.cpp;l\u003d2488;drc\u003dcb899108c8f94f083e50c271d3175af3fe5c0c39.\n\nOne thing I still want to change here is to avoid calling into the audioflinger for a cleanup right here. It would be better if we just create the patch release command and enqueue it. This has two benefits: 1) reuse of the existing code for patch release handling, and 2) better responsiveness of the loop to exit requests.",
